    "stations": {
      "description": "How the stations move: every station round a planet or moon, port and environmental, circles it, paced as real orbits are, so far stations turn slower and move slower (Book: Docking at stations). Orbits may pass through other bodies and each other: nothing collides. Ships docked at a station, and landing or launching there, move with it; full assist holds still relative to one as you near it. Planets, moons and the stars hold still, and so, unless starPeriod is set, do the stations round a star.",
